# Agent instructions

This project uses the ai-kit workflow (Claude Code + Cursor).

**Context budget**: lean on `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/adr/` as cached truth — don't re-derive what's already documented. For wide codebase sweeps, delegate to a sub-agent (`Explore`, `Plan`) so raw output stays out of the main conversation. Full rule: `.cursor/rules/context-discipline.mdc` (or `standards/rules/context-discipline.mini.md` in ai-kit).

## Agile lifecycle

| Fase | Doel | Skills |
| ---- | ---- | ------ |
| **Ideation** | Scope, requirements, alignment | `grill-me`, `grill-with-docs`, `to-prd`, `prototype`, `zoom-out` |
| **Development** | Backlog → incrementeel bouwen | `to-issues` → `triage` → `tdd` (+ Sandcastle voor AFK) |
| **Testing** | Continuous test & fix | `tdd`, `review`, `qa`, `diagnose` |
| **Deployment** | Release naar productie | `ship` |
| **Ops & Review** | Feedback, retrospective | `retro` |

One-off: `setup` (onboarding), `handoff` (agent context), `improve-codebase-architecture` (brownfield).

Framework (Scrum/Kanban): see `docs/agents/workflow.md`.

Run **`/setup`** once — configures dev environment, Docker, tracker, labels, domain docs, agile workflow.

Setup status: `.ai-kit-setup` (committed after `/setup`).

